{"name":"Porch Swing","hex":"#597175","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"porch swing","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of swing, often made of wood and having space for two people to sit and rock back and forth. A porch swing is often connected to the roof of the porch with chains and hooks in the ceiling but may also hang from a self-standing frame."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/porch_swing"}],"entries":[{"title":"Swing (seat)","blocks":[{"text":"A swing is a seat or platform, suspended from chains, ropes, or bars, on which one or more people can swing back and forth for enjoyment or relaxation. Swings are a common piece of equipment at children's playgrounds and may also be found in yards or gardens, on porches, inside homes, or as freestanding public play equipment like the Estonian village swing. Swings have a long history in many different parts of the world and come in various types."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/MoSchaukel.jpg/330px-MoSchaukel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swing_(seat)","wikidata":"Q188688"},{"title":"Porch","blocks":[{"text":"A porch is a room or gallery located in front of an entrance to a building. A porch is placed in front of the façade of a building it commands, and forms a low front. Alternatively, it may be a vestibule or a projecting building that houses the entrance door of a building."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Chartres_Cathedral_020_south_facade_TTaylor.JPG/330px-Chartres_Cathedral_020_south_facade_TTaylor.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porch","wikidata":"Q816741"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Tire_swing%2C_near_Litchfield%2C_Connecticut_LCCN2012630791.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Tire_swing%